{"question_id": "test_00070", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "A", "explanation": "The patient has alcoholic liver cirrhosis with ascites, fever, and hepatic encephalopathy (elevated ammonia, asterixis, altered mental status). Spontaneous bacterial peritonitis (SBP) is a common precipitating factor for encephalopathy in cirrhotic patients with ascites, especially when fever is present. Evidence [3] describes ascites in cirrhosis but does not directly mention SBP; however, the clinical presentation strongly supports infection as the trigger. Other options are less likely: metabolic alkalosis is absent (normal ABG), portal vein thrombosis would likely cause variceal bleeding (not seen), and hypoglycemia is not present (glucose 90 mg/dL).", "confidence": 0.85, "gold_answer": "A", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 14550.419092178345, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1459, "output": 674}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_3641", "InternalMed_Harrison_3664", "InternalMed_Harrison_24044", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1112", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5216"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 639.3945217132568, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 13910.786867141724, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1459, "output": 674}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
{"question_id": "test_00071", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "A", "explanation": "The patient's chest pain, sinus tachycardia, elevated troponins, and elevated pulmonary capillary wedge pressure after blunt chest trauma from a motor vehicle collision are classic for cardiac contusion. Evidence [1] and [2] discuss chest pain evaluation and high-risk cardiopulmonary causes, but the specific trauma context and elevated troponins point to myocardial injury from contusion rather than hemorrhage, pulmonary contusion, or Takotsubo cardiomyopathy.", "confidence": 0.9, "gold_answer": "A", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 4383.290529251099, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1236, "output": 112}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_1385", "InternalMed_Harrison_1342", "InternalMed_Harrison_24358", "InternalMed_Harrison_20167", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4939"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 560.3406429290771, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 3822.728395462036, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1236, "output": 112}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
{"question_id": "test_00072", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "C", "explanation": "The patient's acute kidney injury, oliguria, low urine sodium, and hyponatremia in the setting of cirrhosis and ascites are consistent with hepatorenal syndrome (HRS). The definitive treatment for HRS is liver transplantation. Among the options, dopamine is not effective, lisinopril may worsen renal function, and TIPS is not first-line and may be contraindicated. Thus, liver transplantation is the best option.", "confidence": 0.85, "gold_answer": "C", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 8295.686721801758, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1580, "output": 589}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_3641", "InternalMed_Harrison_3664", "InternalMed_Harrison_3617", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5216", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5601"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 634.5791816711426, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 7660.89129447937, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1580, "output": 589}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
{"question_id": "test_00073", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "B", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms (weight loss, heat intolerance, tachycardia, hypertension, warm moist skin, fine tremor) are classic for hyperthyroidism, likely Graves' disease. Methimazole is a first-line antithyroid medication for young patients, as it directly reduces thyroid hormone production. Propranolol only controls symptoms, radioiodine is typically reserved for older patients or those who fail medications, and glucocorticoids are not standard initial therapy. Evidence [1] supports methimazole use in similar cases, though it notes radioiodine after poor adherence.", "confidence": 0.95, "gold_answer": "B", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 8436.743974685669, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1073, "output": 786}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_4230", "Gynecology_Novak_6481", "InternalMed_Harrison_19572", "InternalMed_Harrison_3173", "InternalMed_Harrison_27709"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 594.6381092071533, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 7841.898679733276, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1073, "output": 786}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
