{"question_id": "test_00107", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "A", "explanation": "The patient's presentation is consistent with Klinefelter syndrome (47,XXY), which can result from paternal nondisjunction during spermatogenesis. Nondisjunction most commonly occurs in meiosis I, which takes place in the primary spermatocyte stage. The evidence describes Klinefelter syndrome features (small testes, gynecomastia, tall stature, infertility) and that genetic abnormalities are a cause of male infertility, but does not specify the stage of nondisjunction. Based on standard medical knowledge, the error most likely occurs in the primary spermatocyte.", "confidence": 0.7, "gold_answer": "A", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 18681.58006668091, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1145, "output": 2249}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_27599", "InternalMed_Harrison_27240", "InternalMed_Harrison_27241", "InternalMed_Harrison_27324", "Histology_Ross_3702"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 819.3237781524658, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 17862.0285987854, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1145, "output": 2249}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
