{"question_id": "test_00148", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "B", "explanation": "The patient presents with early prominent behavioral changes (inappropriate language, grabbing, disinhibition) and language difficulty, progressing to memory loss, which is typical of frontotemporal dementia. The provided evidence does not directly address dementia subtypes, but the clinical picture aligns with frontotemporal dementia rather than Alzheimer's (which typically presents with early memory loss), Kluver-Bucy syndrome (rare with hyperorality/hypersexuality), or vascular dementia (stepwise decline with focal signs). Hypertension is present but not specific.", "confidence": 0.7, "gold_answer": "B", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 8919.675827026367, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1133, "output": 866}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_6619", "Pharmacology_Katzung_914", "InternalMed_Harrison_9716", "InternalMed_Harrison_10248", "InternalMed_Harrison_32487"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 600.7463932037354, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 8318.715572357178, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1133, "output": 866}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
{"question_id": "test_00149", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "A", "explanation": "Staphylococcal scalded-skin syndrome is caused by exfoliative toxin from S. aureus. The primary defense against bacterial toxins involves IgG antibodies, which neutralize toxins and opsonize bacteria. Evidence does not specify the immunoglobulin class, but IgG is the main antibody for systemic toxin neutralization.", "confidence": 0.8, "gold_answer": "D", "is_correct": false, "total_latency_ms": 17242.72894859314, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1386, "output": 84}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_1645", "InternalMed_Harrison_11698", "First_Aid_Step2_138", "InternalMed_Harrison_4109", "InternalMed_Harrison_10339"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 685.7171058654785, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 16556.782722473145, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1386, "output": 84}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
{"question_id": "test_00150", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "A", "explanation": "The patient presents with community-acquired pneumonia (CAP) with atypical features (dry cough, diarrhea, hyponatremia) suggestive of Legionella or other atypical pathogens. Levofloxacin is a fluoroquinolone effective against typical and atypical respiratory pathogens, including Legionella, and is appropriate empiric therapy for CAP. Amoxicillin is not first-line due to resistance, trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole is for Pneumocystis pneumonia (not indicated here), and rifampin is for tuberculosis (not suspected). Evidence [1] supports empiric antibiotics for pneumonia, and the clinical picture aligns with levofloxacin use.", "confidence": 0.9, "gold_answer": "A", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 55069.82517242432, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1377, "output": 707}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_4939", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5216", "InternalMed_Harrison_3630", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5601", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_144"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 636.3673210144043, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 54433.22730064392, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1377, "output": 707}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
{"question_id": "test_00151", "variant": "v1", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "D", "explanation": "The ultrasound describes bilateral enlarged ovaries with multiple thin-walled, septated cysts containing clear fluid. This is characteristic of theca lutein cysts, which are often associated with high hCG levels (e.g., molar pregnancy). The intrauterine heteroechoic mass with numerous anechoic spaces and no fetus or amniotic fluid suggests a hydatidiform mole, which is a common cause of theca lutein cysts. Evidence does not describe chocolate cysts (endometriomas) as thin-walled with clear fluid; they have ground-glass echogenicity. Corpus luteum cysts are usually unilateral and not typically multiple thin-walled septated cysts. Yolk sac tumor is a malignant germ cell tumor, not associated with this sonographic pattern.", "confidence": 0.95, "gold_answer": "D", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 4552.202224731445, "total_token_usage": {"input": 1101, "output": 172}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": ["Gynecology_Novak_2088", "Obstentrics_Williams_8654", "Gynecology_Novak_2600", "Obstentrics_Williams_8656", "Obstentrics_Williams_2539"], "retrieval_latency_ms": 725.9321212768555, "retrieval_token_usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0}, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 3826.066017150879, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 1101, "output": 172}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
